# Svdown

Renders Markdown from an AI response while it streams. Pass the text received so far as `content` and append to it as chunks arrive. New text is typed out, code fences become highlighted code blocks, and `<SvThink>`, `<SvPlan>`, and `<SvFiles>` blocks show as activity steps.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Svdown } from "#lib/components/ui/svdown/index.js";

	let content = $state("");

	// Append each chunk as it arrives from the model.
	async function ask() {
		const response = await fetch("/api/chat", { method: "POST" });
		const reader = response.body!.pipeThrough(new TextDecoderStream()).getReader();
		while (true) {
			const { done, value } = await reader.read();
			if (done) break;
			content += value;
		}
	}
</script>

<Svdown {content} />
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/svdown.json
```

## Markdown

Headings, paragraphs, emphasis, strikethrough, inline code, links, images, blockquotes, ordered, unordered, and task lists, tables, and dividers follow GitHub Flavored Markdown. Wide tables scroll sideways.

Svdown does not style the Markdown itself. Each run of prose renders in a `typeset typeset-chat` wrapper, styled by `typeset.css`, which installs with this component. Import it once in your root layout. Change the fonts, line height, and spacing for chat responses in the `.typeset-chat` rule at the top of that file.

```svelte title="+layout.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import "../styles/typeset.css";
</script>
```

Code fences render with `CodeBlock`. Add a `path` after the language, such as `svelte path="src/App.svelte"`, to show it in the header. Add line numbers in braces, such as `ts {1,3-5}`, to highlight those lines. Languages without highlighting show as plain text.

## Streaming

Appended text is typed out a few characters at a time, faster when it falls behind. Replacing `content` with text that does not start with the old text, such as a new message, shows it at once. Set `removeAnimation` to show text at once, such as for earlier messages. People who prefer reduced motion always see text at once.

A custom tag that is still arriving, such as `<SvTh`, stays hidden until it is complete.

## Activity blocks

Wrap reasoning in `<SvThink>` and a plan in `<SvPlan>` to show them as an `AIAction` step. The step shimmers and stays open while the block streams, and closes once its closing tag arrives.

Wrap code fences with a `path` in `<SvFiles>` to show the files being written, with a spinner on the current one. An optional `title` attribute replaces the step title. Set `onFileClick` to run code when a file is clicked, `onFiles` to receive the block while it streams, or `renderFiles` to render the block yourself.

<Demo section="files" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Svdown {content} onFileClick={(path) => openFile(path)} />
```

## Safety

Model output is untrusted, so raw HTML shows as text by default and cannot run scripts. Links and images keep only relative addresses and the `http`, `https`, `mailto`, and `tel` schemes; others, such as `javascript:`, are dropped. Set `allowHtml` only for content you trust.

<Demo section="html" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Svdown content={trustedMarkdown} allowHtml />
```

## Extensions

`svdownMarked` is the Marked instance Svdown parses with. Add your own extensions with `svdownMarked.use()`, and render their tokens with the `renderCustom` snippet. `getSvdownTokens` and `getFilesBlockDataFromSvdown` parse Markdown without rendering it.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Svdown {content}>
	{#snippet renderCustom(token)}
		<p>Custom token: {token.type}</p>
	{/snippet}
</Svdown>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg` to change the typeset text size, the spacing between blocks, and the size of the code blocks and activity steps. It defaults to `md`. Setting `--typeset-size` in the `.typeset-chat` rule overrides it.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Svdown size="sm" {content} />
```

## API

`Svdown` extends the `div` attributes. Extra attributes pass through.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompProps<"div"> {
	/** Markdown source; append to it as the response streams */
	content: string;
	/** Shows new text at once instead of typing it out; reduced motion always shows it at once */
	removeAnimation?: boolean;
	/** Renders raw HTML in the Markdown; off by default, so HTML shows as text and cannot run scripts */
	allowHtml?: boolean;
	/** Called with a file's path when it is clicked in the default files list */
	onFileClick?: (path: string) => void;
	/** Called with the files block while it is still streaming */
	onFiles?: (data: FilesToken) => void;
	/** Replaces the default files list for each files block */
	renderFiles?: Snippet<[FilesToken]>;
	/** Renders tokens from Marked extensions you add with `svdownMarked.use()` */
	renderCustom?: Snippet<[Tokens.Generic]>;
	/** Typeset text size, spacing between blocks, and the size of the code blocks and activities; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
}
```
